 "notes": [
  {
   "book": 1,
   "row": 230,
   "sec": 4,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Roots of trusteeship:** Gandhi drew the idea from the Gita's teaching of non-possession (aparigraha) and from the English law of trusts (Snell's Equity), as he tells in his autobiography."
  },
  {
   "book": 1,
   "row": 232,
   "sec": 7,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **The ground:** Jallianwala Bagh was a walled garden, closed in by houses and walls, with only one narrow way in and out."
  }
